	)
	(text "IS66WVS4M8BLL-104NLI : 32 Mbit (4M x 8) QPI PSRAM.\nALL = 1.8 V part, BLL = 3.0 V part - BLL is the 3V3-compatible one.\n104 MHz, 50 ohm output drive: point to point, no series termination.\nCE# pull-up keeps the device deselected while the MCU pins are hi-Z.\nNO TEST POINTS ON THIS BUS - DEC-0018 ruling 1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 128.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "355bf054-d4ef-5bbd-a8e9-560194fd18ce")
	)
	(text "A  MCU CORE - SUPPLIES, RESET, BOOT, HSE CLOCK IN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 13.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3e4f7de9-9198-59b4-b783-f182fe446e5e")
	)
	(text "USB3320C-EZK-TR, ULPI OUTPUT CLOCK mode: the PHY generates the 60 MHz\nULPI clock on CLKOUT -> STM32 ULPI_CK (PA5).  Its 24 MHz reference is\nits OWN crystal on REFCLK / XO (block C) - no clock is shared with the\nSTM32.  REFSEL[2:0]=111 still selects 24 MHz (DS Table 5-10).  RBIAS\n8.06k 1% and RVBUS 10k (device-only) are datasheet-mandated values\n(DS 2.1, Table 5-7).  ID tied to VDD33 = device-only operation\n(DS 5.6.1).  CPEN / SPK_L / SPK_R / N-C are unused: no OTG VBUS\nswitch, no audio.  RESETB has no internal pull-down - the 10k holds\nthe PHY in reset while the STM32 pins are hi-Z, which also covers the\nVDD18-before-VDDIO sequence note.\nNO TEST POINTS ON THE ULPI BUS - DEC-0018 ruling 1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204.47 92.71 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "482d4309-721b-5ff9-a112-6ea5867396ac")
	)
	(text "F  USB3320C Hi-SPEED ULPI PHY  (REQ-AR-13)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.58 13.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
