	(text "Six through-hole GND loops, spread across the board at layout so an\noscilloscope ground clip is never far from the signal hook being probed.\nThe house standard asks for these wherever TestPointHook is used, and the\nblock sheets use hooks on I2C1, SPI2, SPI3 and the fault lines."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 318.77 297.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8b9d8b0c-6ac7-54dd-a1dc-024cc568781d")
	)
	(text "The USB3320 has its own 24 MHz reference: an ECS-240-12-23G-JGN-TR crystal on\nthe PHY's internal oscillator between REFCLK and XO (DS Figure 5-4). It shares\nnothing with the STM32 HSE oscillator in block B. REFSEL[2:0] = 111 still\nselects a 24 MHz reference (DS Table 5-10), so no configuration changes.\n\nCrystal: fundamental, parallel resonant, CL 18 pF, -40 to +85 C. DS Table 4-11\nasks for CL 20 pF typ, ESR <= 30 ohm and a +/-500 ppm total budget - CONFIRM\nthe ECS-23G ESR against 30 ohm before the first order.\nLoad caps: C = 2 x (CL - Cstray) = 2 x (18 - 5) = 26 pF -> 27 pF C0G 2%, with\nCstray = 3 pF pin capacitance (DS Table 4-11) + ~2 pF PCB per side.\n\nLAYOUT: crystal and both load caps within a few mm of pins 25 / 26, ground\nguard under the part, no other traces beneath it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 414.02 52.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "97504546-d7ef-5f56-9ebb-1d46dad392f4")
	)
	(text "PINOUT - the STM32 14-way 1.27 mm IDC order, copied pin for pin\nfrom ARIA_EITSYS_CBs_1 (Microcontroller.kicad_sch, J11) so one\ndebug cable serves both boards:\n  1  NC       2  NC       3  VDD (+3V3 via R1015 100R)\n  4  SWDIO    5  GND      6  SWCLK    7  GND\n  8  NC       9  NC      10  SWO     11  GND\n 12  nRESET  13  DBG_RX  14  DBG_TX\n\nSWO on pin 10 is this board's ONE addition: pin 10 is NC on the\nreference board, this design has SWO (REQ-AR-15), and a cable\nwired for that board just leaves it open.\nUSART3 shares the header, as REQ-AR-15 and the block diagram both\nask. It is SWD-safe: a probe drives 4, 6 and 12 and reads 10, and\nthe .ioc sets Trace_Asynchronous_SW so PB4 / PB3 are not JTAG.\nR1013 / R1014 / R1015, 100R each, make a mis-plugged probe or a\nshorted console pin a nuisance rather than damage.\n\nDBG_TX / DBG_RX keep the .ioc net names: DBG_TX is the STM32\nOUTPUT (USART3_TX, PD8), DBG_RX the STM32 INPUT (USART3_RX, PD9).\nMCU_nRESET comes from block A, which owns its 100 nF, its push\nbutton and its test point. All six debug nets are sheet-local now\nthat the header sits on the page it serves."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 497.84 99.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a6619c14-faa8-53a5-8b98-35b97dff613e")
	)
	(text "H  SWD + USART3 DEBUG HEADER  (REQ-AR-15)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 412.75 93.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b64e1d58-e49f-5be6-a1b0-5d1ffab9276b")
	)
	(text "TEST ACCESS (TEST_PLAN 4). The whole test_debug sheet lives here now: block H\nis the SWD + USART3 debug header, J the rail probe header, K the GND hooks.\nTest coverage belongs on the page it covers, not on a sheet of its own -\ndocs/decisions/actuator-rev-testdebug.md.\nOther TPs: NRST (hook), BOOT0, HSE clock (dual TP, block B), +3V3_USB and\n+1V8_USB (block E). MCO2 leaves the sheet as ADS1235_CLKIN and is probed in\nloadcell_afe, which owns that net's break. Supply-pin groups are reachable at\nthe decoupling banks in blocks A, D, E and F.\nDELIBERATELY NO test points on ULPI or OCTOSPI (DEC-0018 ruling 1 / TP 2.2).\n\nROOT SHEET. Every hierarchical label on this sheet is a sheet pin on the mcu\nblock of the root. SWDIO, SWCLK, SWO, MCU_nRESET, DBG_TX and DBG_RX are no\nlonger among them - they became sheet-local when test_debug was dissolved,\nand their sheet pins came off the root with it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 329 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b940b122-2175-5be6-af8d-a093faa1f973")
	)
	(text "STM32H723VET6 + USB3320 ULPI PHY + USB-C (data only) + OCTOSPI1 PSRAM,\nwith the board's debug and bring-up access alongside it (blocks H, J, K).\nPin map authority: hardware/cubemx/ARIA_SRB_FAFF_2_POC_CBs_1.ioc\n(DEC-0013) - nothing here re-pins it.\n\nLocal labels stay on this sheet: ULPI_*, QSPI_P1_*, USB_*, HSE_CLK_24M,\nUSB_REFCLK_24M, USB_XO_24M, USB3320_nRESET, SPARE_*, +3V3_USB, +1V8_USB -\nand now SWDIO, SWCLK, SWO, MCU_nRESET, DBG_TX and DBG_RX as well, because\nthe header that consumes them is on this sheet and they no longer leave it.\nHierarchical labels leave it; the full list and every direction is in\ndocs/decisions/actuator-sch-mcu.md.\n\nPC2_C / PC3_C carry ULPI_DIR and ULPI_NXT: firmware MUST close the\nSYSCFG_PMCR analog switch (PC2SO / PC3SO) before the ULPI link will run -\nthe pins are otherwise isolated from the digital I/O. DS13313 6.3.16 Tbl 56."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 295.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c180b6c8-22db-5e87-a94d-fff74ce0ec3f")
	)
	(text "VDD: 5 x 100nF + a 4u7 bulk, one cap per supply pin group.\nVDDA / VREF+: 2 x 100nF + 2 x 1uF.  VCAP: 2 x 2u2, ESR < 100 mOhm\n(DS13313 Table 14).  NRST: 100nF, per DS13313 Figure 18.\nVSSA is tied to the board GND here; the precision analogue ground\nstrategy belongs to power_rails / loadcell_afe (ARCHITECTURE 5.3)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 68.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cdb22689-c1c8-551e-be2a-ad29fcf382ff")
	)
	(text "USB 2.0 data only: no VBUS load, no sink, no PD (REQ-EL-10, DEC-0002).\n5.1k Rd on both CC lines is what makes this a valid USB-C device\nattachment. VBUS is SENSED ONLY, through RVBUS in block F, so the PHY\nSessVld comparator tells firmware a host is present - which is why\nVBUS_MON (PC5) stays free for the motor DC link (supports OQ-01 /\nDEC-0011). CC carries nothing but the two Rd resistors, so it needs no\nESD part; the high-speed pair has the USBLC6-2P6."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 316.23 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d3cac05c-5baf-511d-8501-ad9679a2a047")
	)
	(text "G  USB-C RECEPTACLE - DATA ONLY, NO BUS POWER, NO PD"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 298.45 13.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d70fbf18-5cd5-5572-bddf-e4857e250f10")
	)
	(text "24 MHz LVCMOS MEMS oscillator, 10 ppm, driving the STM32 HSE\nONLY - the USB3320 now has its own crystal (block C), so the\ntwo clock domains share nothing.  STM32 HSE is an EXTERNAL\nCLOCK on PH0 (PH1-OSC_OUT unallocated in the .ioc, REQ-AR-16),\nso no bare crystal here.  33R source-terminates the one trace."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 125.73 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e2b29cd5-43b7-544d-ab90-4a42ec44931b")
	)
	(text "Ten MCU pins are unallocated in the .ioc. Seven of them are brought\nout here so a wire mod can serve OQ-06 (EEPROM nWP) and OQ-07 (rail\nPGOOD / enable) without a board spin. DNP by default - fit only if\nneeded. PC14/PC15 (OSC32) and PH1-OSC_OUT are left unconnected so a\n32.768 kHz LSE remains possible on a later revision."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 232.41 254 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f29dd1ed-cafc-51da-8aee-607cfd2700c8")
	)
	(text "MCU PORTS - PIN ASSIGNMENT IS THE .ioc (DEC-0013); ULPI / QSPI / USB3320_nRESET / SPARE_* stay on this sheet"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 153.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fde5e7d4-22a8-5642-b6f7-0a7c75876eb2")
	)
